From af0ce879f4149002117a4a2fe0bfda217ed1a6a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luo Jie <jie.luo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 03:22:49 -0700
Subject: arm64: dts: qcom: ipq5018: Enable mdio0 for SoC-integrated EPHY

mdio0 is the internal MDIO bus used to access the SoC-integrated
EPHY (ge_phy), which is present on every IPQ5018 RDP board. Enable
mdio0 with a 6.25MHz MDIO clock in the SoC dtsi so all boards can
reach the EPHY, instead of enabling it per board.

Signed-off-by: Luo Jie <jie.luo@oss.qualcomm.com>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260902-qcom_ipq5018_mdio_pinctrl-v3-2-629c7bb05c44@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Bjorn Andersson <andersson@kernel.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

(limited to 'arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi')

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/ipq5018.dtsi
@@ -222,8 +222,7 @@
 
 			clocks = <&gcc GCC_MDIO0_AHB_CLK>;
 			clock-names = "gcc_mdio_ahb_clk";
-
-			status = "disabled";
+			clock-frequency = <6250000>;
 
 			ge_phy: ethernet-phy@7 {
 				compatible = "ethernet-phy-id004d.d0c0";
